Just like vector, list is a type of container which stores different types of elements
its a bidirectional linear container. The difference between a list and an array is
when we store elements inside an array, the memory of the elements become contagious. That is,
if you want to remove an element from the array, you have to shift the other elements into the
removed elments. But thats not the case of the list. In list, you can remove or add elements 
without thinking of the 'contagious' behavior of the memory. 

The thumb rule is, if you want to insert and delete elements in a fast and efficient way, then
use list. Otherwise, use array. 

The examples will show different syntaxes of list.